 ## Shared principles
-All methods in this family compute the expected color $\hat{C}(r)$ for a ray $r$ by discretizing the medium interaction interval into steps and accumulating emission weighted by transmittance [S1, unofficial]. The core mathematical formulation relies on the Beer-Lambert law to convert volume density $\sigma$ into opacity $\alpha$ and transmittance $T$.
